WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.035
Well, the fallout continues

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.303
tonight for President Biden

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.037
and White House

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.605
staff over the mishandling

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.073
of classified information

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.842
and lack of transparency.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.377
CNN senior political commentator

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.178
Adam Kinzinger joins us now with more.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.947
So, Adam Reuters.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.182
Jeff Mason says this probe, quote,

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.451
has neutralized Democrats ability

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.787
to target former President Trump.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.721
Former Obama

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.156
adviser David Axelrod

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.291
calls it a huge gift to Trump.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.160
What's your take?

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.962
Yeah, I think they're right.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:29.763
It's a huge gift.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.464
So there's the legal side

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.799
and there's the political side.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.701
The legal side will be

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.369
the legal side can do nuance.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.270
They'll be fair.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.072
They'll go through

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.874
the Donald Trump thing,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.876
the Joe Biden thing, and go after it

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.612
the right way politically.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.013
Basically, this is taken out,

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.581
I think, almost any ability

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.315
for Democrats

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.051
to go after the former

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.652
president on this issue.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.019
Still,

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.754
there is still a January 6th thing

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.221
that happened,

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.022
which I think is important

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.157
to keep in mind.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.459
And it's really about me.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.593
The other thing is that

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.028
I think one of the biggest problems

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.829
has been

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.230
the continuing

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.366
revelation of new documents.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.468
And they've not done a good job

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.503
of putting together how that happened

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.539
or they continue it finding new batches.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.374
Did they happen upon it?

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.909
And I think politically,

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.610
it's pretty bad at the moment.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:17.844
Yeah.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.612
When they released the first statement

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.548
talking about the batch in November,

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.850
it failed to mention the second batch

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.385
that was found in December.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.820
So then they had the

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.421
reporters found out about it.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.823
They released another statement.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.691
So there are certainly fair questions

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.493
about a lack of transparency

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.794
from the Biden White House.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.062
But let's listen to what House

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.830
Oversight Chairman

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.032
James Colmer said to me in November

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.967
regarding the classified documents

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.336
found at Trump's residence and Mar a Lago

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.773
I don't know much about that.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.274
That's not something that

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.576
we've requested information

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.977
just to see what was going on,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:51.544
because I don't

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.681
know what documents were at Mar-A-Lago

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:55.982
So, you know,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.483
that's something

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.151
we're just waiting to see

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.252
what comes out in that.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.453
But is it fair to say

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.689
that investigation won't be a priority?

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.458
That will not be a priority.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:05.959
Okay.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.460
So that was about Trump.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.761
And now this is what he said

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.529
earlier today

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.499
about the Biden investigation.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.500
At the end of the day.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.400
My biggest concern

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.802
is that the classified documents,

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.636
to be honest with you,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.271
my concern is how

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.073
there's such a discrepancy

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:20.840
in how former

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.541
President Trump

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.976
was treated by raiding Mar

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:23.510
a Lago, by

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.011
getting the security cameras,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.913
by taking pictures of documents

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.448
on the on the floor, by going through

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.984
Melania's closet versus Joe Biden.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:31.251
They're like,

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.986
okay, your personal lawyers,

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.954
you don't have security clearance.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.289
They can go through.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.690
They can just keep looking

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.024
and keep

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.292
looking and,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.027
you know, determine whatever is there

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.129
that's not equal treatment.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.901
What do you make of that?

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:48.902
Well, first off,

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.637
thank you for keeping that

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.371
and playing it,

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.039
because I think this is very important

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.073
for people to see

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.242
as, frankly, the hypocrisy that exists.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.111
And secondarily,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.746
it's a very different situation.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.848
I think a lot of people forget that

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.283
Mar a Lago was raided

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.351
only after repeated engagements

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.286
with the government.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.720
They said, we know you have this,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.655
they know they've moved it.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.156
They've said we don't have it.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.591
And that's what led to this.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.293
So it's a different situation.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.727
But as Mr.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.396
Komar is doing

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.564
and doing quite well,

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.133
if you throw enough stuff on the wall,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.601
it creates a lot of confusion.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.069
But but I think the bottom line

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.705
is anybody, whether you're a Republican

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.840
or a Democrat talking about this issue,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.776
you should be consistent

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:30.510
with what you said

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.844
about Donald Trump as well.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.780
There are differences, you can note that.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.547
But this is one of the

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.615
things that drives me

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.250
and I think a lot of Americans

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.719
crazy is open, obvious

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.554
and almost a disregard

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.456
for whether or not something you say is

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.292
not consistent with what you say

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.260
with a different party.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.729
Just be consistent. Uphold the law.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.898
We can't have classified information

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:52.599
out there

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.366
and investigate

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.935
Donald Trump and Joe Biden.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:56.336
Right.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.904
And that was I remember

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.906
when Republicans came out

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.775
so strongly defending Trump at that time.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.843
It was notable.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.411
And then here you are in a situation

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.145
where the same thing

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.213
is happening with President Biden

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.281
in terms of

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.349
classified documents

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.217
being not where they should be.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:11.985
And suddenly

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.519
they've had to change their tune.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.254
Right into

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.222
it is interesting and important to note.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.124
You've had some pretty dire things

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:18.524
to say

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.892
about the future of your party,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.562
especially after the speaker fight.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.630
And I'm curious,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.497
have you ever considered

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.431
switching parties

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.767
to become an independent

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.403
I mean, those are kinds of thoughts.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.337
You frankly

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:31.871
go through my head

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.206
all the time about, you know,

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.073
what is the future

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.341
of the Republican Party?

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.576
What's you know,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.710
how do I identify

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.812
when it comes to the politics of this?

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.114
I'm still a believer that, look,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.081
I think

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.183
even though things are still continuing

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:44.884
to go off the rails

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.085
with the Republican Party,

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.388
there are signs with the lessening

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.922
of Donald Trump's influence,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.890
although I think people have

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.292
learned Trumpism,

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.126
there is signs

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:53.893
that some of this may

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.329
eventually burn itself out.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.231
And so I'll never say

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.199
I quit considering it, because for me

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:00.633
and I think that's

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.735
how most Americans feel, is like

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.004
you just want to be represented

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.039
by somebody.

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:07.173
And in my case,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.174
the Republican Party

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.642
has certainly felt like it's left me.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.511
I would change my policies, my beliefs

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.378
or anything.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.680
I just believe in truth.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.881
And I believe in being committed

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.016
to truth and consistency and honesty.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:17.750
And that's where I feel

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.418
a little homeless

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.553
in the Republican Party sometimes.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:23.456
But you still identify as a Republican.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.158
What would be the final straw for you?

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.628
I think it's like when it happens,

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:29.829
that'll be the final straw.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.597
When, you know, you know, look, it's

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.466
we are still a country represented

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.234
by two political parties generally.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.203
And obviously, there's minor parties.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.305
And I think the Republican Party

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.540
still deserves a fight

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.507
for the soul of it.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.809
But, you know,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.043
at the same time,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.713
I think most Americans feel like I'm

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:47.880
kind of tired of voting

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.182
for lesser of two evils.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.683
And so right now, I'm

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.552
enjoying not being in Congress,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.986
and I'll continue

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.322
to evaluate that with myself. Every day.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.024
Well, let's talk about a Republican

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.292
that is in Congress right now,

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.393
and that would be

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:01.794
the New York Congressman,

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:02.929
George Santos,

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.931
who has lied about his identity

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.367
The voters put him in office

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.236
based on an identity that he made up.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.437
And we're getting more

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.405
and more evidence

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.473
of everything he made up,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.841
it seems like, by the day

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:16.409
here is the latest example.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.978
This was a radio interview he did

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.446
where he fabricated

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.215
playing on a volleyball team,

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.349
going to Baruch College

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.650
and getting surgery. Let's listen

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:27.587
You know,

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.789
it's funny, I actually went to school on

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:32.091
on a volleyball scholarship. I did.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.359
I know what I did.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:33.960
Yeah,

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.628
when I was in Peru,

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.263
we were the number one volleyball.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.364
You graduate from the.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.198
Did you graduate from there?

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.234
Yeah. So did I did. I did. So did I.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:41.768
Very cool.

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.436
A great school, great institution.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:44.971
Very good. Very good.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.973
I look, I sacrifice both my knees

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.275
and got very nice. Knee replacement.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.177
Knee replacement from outside

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.412
playing volleyball.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:55.381
That's how serious I took the game.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:57.950
Again, a ally.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.152
Your thoughts?

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:01.788
And you don't serve me, by the way.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.089
Kevin McCarthy.

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:03.623
Oh, go ahead.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:04.724
I just want to note to our viewers,

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:05.324
he is still serving

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.627
Kevin McCarthy has said he has no plans

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:09.662
to ask him to resign, but go ahead.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.097
Although other Republicans have.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:11.731
Yeah,

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.032
I mean, look, Kevin

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.300
can't ask him to resign

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.568
because Kevin needs his vote

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.403
as it is right now.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.272
I really worry about the Republicans

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:20.306
ability to pass anything.

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:21.841
I worry about the country's ability

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.543
to pass something through the debt limit.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:26.179
This guy is not just

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:27.680
expanding his resume.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.282
He's not lying about some things.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:29.949
I mean, truthfully,

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:33.352
he is a total utter fraud in his election

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.354
in front of the people of New York

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:36.422
was fraudulent.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.890
He presented himself

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.325
as somebody he wasn't.

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.127
Look, I don't think he

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.662
I don't think he can make it

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:43.796
two years in Congress

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:44.630
just personally

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.065
I mean, Congress can kick him out,

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:46.599
by the way.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:49.502
Congress can certainly censure

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.003
it. Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.004
There has to be a big majority.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.139
And I think if Kevin came out

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.507
and was for it, they would do it.

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:57.043
But Kevin McCarthy needs his vote.

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.244
This I feel bad

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:00.279
for the 700,000 people in New York

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.380
that he represents, that

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.281
he utterly,

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.617
absolutely, completely lied to.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:06.452
So then.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:06.886
Okay,

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:08.554
so so clearly you have issues with him,

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:09.689
but what is your message to Kevin

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:10.823
McCarthy then about this?

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:13.426
Well, I mean,

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:13.960
look, if I was

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.261
there, I'd tell Kevin, we have to

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:16.662
we have to ask, what are we?

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.064
We have to ask him to resign.

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:18.731
Look, his own

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.233
party back in New York

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.535
has said we want him out.

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.570
I think, you know, if Kevin came out

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.171
and said this,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.606
the leadership of the GOP

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:27.874
in the House, Senate,

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.209
he would maybe he still wouldn't resign.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.744
But I certainly think the pressure

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:32.311
would be there.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:32.912
Look,

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.780
my party has a problem

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.215
with telling the truth.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:38.518
This is not helping that reputation.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.586
And that's what I'd be advising.

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.121
But it's obvious he's not going to do it

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:42.989
because he needs that vote.

